  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 303 AM EDT Mon Aug 10 2026\n\nA drier Saharan Air Layer settles in Wednesday into Thursday as \nthe ridge axis slides a bit further north along the peninsula of \nFlorida. This will allow for the easterly to southeasterly wind \nflow to persist while the lower relative atmospheric moisture will\nprovide lower convective coverage focused inland in the \nafternoons. The dry air will linger until late in the week when \nthe next burst of tropical moisture begins to arrive from the \nBahamas and Greater Antilles Friday into Saturday. This moisture \nwill allow convective activity to trend closer to seasonal norms \nbased on the current forecast guidance. Another round of drier \ncould emerge late in the weekend to close out the long term \nforecast period.\n\nGiven the relative decrease in showers and storms forecast for a \ngood portion of the long term forecast period, temperatures will \nbegin a warming trend with lower to mid 90s becoming the story \nacross much of the area. Triple digit heat index values are forecast \nand the potential for Heat Advisories will need to be monitored day-\nto-day, particularly over the urbanized areas.",
